# Repo-root .dockerignore — applies to every image whose build context is the
# repo root (axisml-platform and the axisml-system components). Without
# it, `docker build ... <REPO_ROOT>` ships the whole tree (all node_modules, the
# .git history, build artifacts) as context, and the platform frontend stage's
# `COPY axisml-platform/frontend/ ./` would clobber the freshly `pnpm install`ed
# node_modules with the host's.
#
# Keep this to universally-safe excludes only: component Dockerfiles COPY just
# the source trees they need, and the platform image rebuilds the frontend
# bundle in a dedicated stage, so none of the below are required in the context.

# Version control & local tooling
.git
.claude

# Dependencies (rebuilt in-image)
**/node_modules

# Build artifacts (rebuilt in-image)
**/bin
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Editor / OS junk
**/.DS_Store
**/*.local
